WEBVTT

﻿1

00:00:23.958 --> 00:00:27.259
Attention:This is a secure area.
For your own safety move away


00:00:27.261 --> 00:00:29.528
from the spacecraft. Selectees please move 
quickly to your assigned boarding stations.


00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:30.596
Altus Exodus.


00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.200
Welcome aboard Altus Exodus.


00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.371
-Welcome aboard Altus Exodus.
- Move this line faster.


00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.710
Come on!


00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:51.116
Move it. Faster. Move it! Come
on.


00:00:58.592 --> 00:00:59.458
Vasquez.


00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.026
Help!


00:01:01.028 --> 00:01:04.696
-This is Baum.The Crowd is riding.I have men down.
-Stop! Stop!


00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.834
Pebbles. Howell you're with me.


00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.574
31st command. This is Baum. Do you read.


00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:17.142
Dammit!


00:01:17.144 --> 00:01:18.777
I have un authorized personnel
boarding the Albert Einstein.


00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:36.195
In pursuit. Ground that air
support. Close those doors!


00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.335
Freeze! Freeze!


00:01:43.337 --> 00:01:44.803
We just wanna live.


00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.109
Captain. We may have stow aways
on board.


00:01:50.111 --> 00:01:51.777
Emergency launch now!


00:01:51.779 --> 00:01:53.445
Now!


00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.396
Full thrust now.


00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.308
I'm sorry. We can't do that
Lieutenant..


00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.245
Baum Sir. Frank Baum. 31st
tactical command.


00:02:26.247 --> 00:02:28.480
North American joint military.


00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:32.317
Captain Sam Crowe. Activate
autopilot and sleep mode.


00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:36.822
Sir. Those people don't belong
on your ship.


00:02:36.824 --> 00:02:39.224
This is one of humanities lifeboats.


00:02:39.226 --> 00:02:43.562
Some where chosen for needed skills. 
Others were picked by lottery.


00:02:43.564 --> 00:02:45.964
So one human must be just good
as another.


00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.567
Well I have to get back sir.


00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:51.270
My team and I are part of
Earth's defenses.


00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:56.141
TIM activate interface once
we reach cryo.


00:02:56.143 --> 00:02:57.476
Yes Sir.


00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:00.379
We're not going into Cryo Sir.


00:03:00.381 --> 00:03:04.416
You know there is an old sailor
saying Frank.


00:03:04.418 --> 00:03:07.953
"Never jump into a lifeboat until 
you have to jump up into it".


00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:11.056
The war is over. We lost.


00:03:11.058 --> 00:03:13.892
No sir. We are not giving up.


00:03:13.894 --> 00:03:17.196
We've been accelerating at one
"G" ever since we left orbit.


00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:20.232
There is no going back.


00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.704
I wasn't asking, sir.


00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.011
You know what? You can shoot me.


00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:36.315
But you can't change the laws 
of physics.


00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:42.955
We are going to another world. And we will all 
be very happy to have your protection there.


00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:51.296
Altus Exodus, Frank.


00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:56.268
Do you see a red cape, sir?


00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.274
What are you looking at?
Everyone back to work.


00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:22.327
Alright Lieutenant we'll be
putting you in cryo now.


00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.471
I'll hang on to this.


00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.947
Will I dream?


00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.652
Nightmares...


00:04:46.654 --> 00:04:49.354
It will be like no time has pass
at all.


00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:01.546
Come on. Up you go. Come on.


00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:16.187
Come on. Come on. Alright.


00:10:12.445 --> 00:10:13.645
Hey!


00:10:13.647 --> 00:10:15.213
Psst! Over here.


00:10:20.486 --> 00:10:21.820
Take that off.


00:10:22.188 --> 00:10:22.988
What?


00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:24.055
Ssshh!


00:10:24.057 --> 00:10:27.292
You might as well have a
bull's-eye on your back.


00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:33.331
How we - What the hell's going on?


00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:35.066
Who's shooting at us?


00:10:36.302 --> 00:10:37.769
I don't know.


00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:43.908
Let's go. Let's get out of here.


00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:47.812
Come on. Come on.


00:11:03.095 --> 00:11:05.030
I'm going up there to recon.


00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:08.133
You stay here. Take him.


00:11:37.997 --> 00:11:39.798
I thought I told you to stay
back there.


00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.466
You're the one with the gun.


00:12:05.524 --> 00:12:06.891
Come on.


00:12:07.526 --> 00:12:08.326
Come on.


00:12:15.801 --> 00:12:16.968
Frank.


00:12:18.771 --> 00:12:19.904
Frank.


00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.440
Report.


00:12:22.442 --> 00:12:24.609
Howell died in crash.


00:12:24.611 --> 00:12:27.712
I don't know about Vasquez.


00:12:27.714 --> 00:12:30.815
Something's been chasing us but
I couldn't get a good look.


00:12:31.884 --> 00:12:33.418
They took out Vasquez.


00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:38.990
They're big. Some sort of sonic
disrupt or with active camouflage.


00:12:38.992 --> 00:12:41.025
Active camouflage?


00:12:43.662 --> 00:12:45.730
I found these two wondering
after the crash.


00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:50.702
We better get moving. There's a
stream about half a klick away.


00:12:50.704 --> 00:12:51.770
We'll throw them off our trail.


00:12:51.772 --> 00:12:54.539
Why should we follow you?


00:12:55.508 --> 00:12:57.208
I'm the one with the gun.


00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.053
No weapon?


00:13:09.055 --> 00:13:12.457
Lost it in the crash. I got this.


00:13:13.192 --> 00:13:15.093
Could you find anything bigger?


00:13:15.095 --> 00:13:16.561
It's bigger then yours.


00:13:16.563 --> 00:13:17.762
It's not what your mama said.


00:13:19.432 --> 00:13:20.865
Alright.


00:13:21.233 --> 00:13:22.867
Did you see those others?


00:13:22.869 --> 00:13:23.835
The pale skinny ones?


00:13:23.837 --> 00:13:25.436
Yeah I saw them.


00:13:25.438 --> 00:13:28.006
They disappeared quick though. I
don't what they were.


00:13:28.008 --> 00:13:29.908
They looked almost human.


00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.376
Almost.


00:13:45.491 --> 00:13:47.025
Who are you people?


00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:52.564
We are-


00:14:05.544 --> 00:14:08.346
No, no no. Too much noise.
They're harmless.


00:14:10.449 --> 00:14:11.549
Who are you people?


00:14:12.918 --> 00:14:16.054
We're from the Isaac Newton. 
We came in on-


00:14:34.073 --> 00:14:35.874
What the hell was that?


00:14:38.577 --> 00:14:40.245
Come on. Come on.


00:15:00.232 --> 00:15:01.566
Follow the stream.


00:15:01.568 --> 00:15:03.401
I'll bear off and lead them
away.


00:15:03.403 --> 00:15:04.636
With you boss.


00:15:04.638 --> 00:15:06.337
Oh No, you stay with them. 
Keep them moving.


00:15:06.639 --> 00:15:08.006
Watch your 6.


00:15:09.108 --> 00:15:10.675
You! You're T.I.M.


00:15:10.677 --> 00:15:13.711
Yes Sir. I'd be happy to assist
you in anyway I can.


00:15:13.713 --> 00:15:16.047
No, Why is he in charge?


00:15:17.449 --> 00:15:18.917
Come on.


00:15:23.022 --> 00:15:24.322
Come on. Hurry up!


00:15:24.757 --> 00:15:27.458
Sir, I might suggest you would
be safer under these unusual


00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:30.061
circumstances if you were
to lower your voice.


00:15:30.063 --> 00:15:31.462
<i>We want them to follow us!</i>


00:15:31.464 --> 00:15:33.598
Sir, I am programmed to
preserve human life.


00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:38.136
I'll preserve your damn ass
if you don't make some noise!


00:15:38.138 --> 00:15:41.272
As you wish, Sir. I'm happy to
assist you!


00:15:59.091 --> 00:16:00.625
I found a place to hide.


00:17:29.081 --> 00:17:34.285
Who the hell are you people? You weren't on the 
Albert Einstein. And where the hell are we?


00:17:34.287 --> 00:17:36.854
Don't you know? You've got crew.


00:17:36.856 --> 00:17:39.490
You've got that.


00:17:40.059 --> 00:17:41.359
It's ok Honda.


00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.361
We were on the Isaac Newton.


00:17:43.363 --> 00:17:45.329
That was the first Ark to leave.


00:17:45.331 --> 00:17:52.170
Right. We crashed here. We don't
know why. None of our crew survived.


00:17:52.172 --> 00:17:56.374
We were rounded up by the Chameleons. 
Those things that are chasing us.


00:17:56.809 --> 00:18:00.311
Some of us were brought back and
were put in to the um-


00:18:01.513 --> 00:18:07.418
I don't know what to call it. It
was like a prison? a Zoo? a Lab?


00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.520
What does it matter? It has cages.


00:18:09.522 --> 00:18:15.293
It had cages. Until your ship crashed into it. 
Now more of our people are dead.


00:18:15.295 --> 00:18:16.861
But you're free.


00:18:16.863 --> 00:18:19.931
Yeah and now they are hunting us
instead of feeding us.


00:18:20.532 --> 00:18:22.433
Do you want to go back there?


00:18:28.073 --> 00:18:29.340
No.


00:18:31.043 --> 00:18:33.277
I didn't think so.


00:18:33.279 --> 00:18:34.779
Now we have to work together.


00:18:34.781 --> 00:18:37.815
To do what? We don't even know
where we are.


00:18:38.484 --> 00:18:40.318
Captain, do you know where we are?


00:18:40.786 --> 00:18:42.353
I-


00:18:42.355 --> 00:18:46.757
This can't be Alpha Proxima 5.
There's only one sun.


00:18:47.259 --> 00:18:49.060
Where...


00:18:49.995 --> 00:18:53.731
It's the head wound. Probably a concussion.


00:18:53.733 --> 00:18:54.866
You a doctor?


00:18:55.367 --> 00:18:58.336
I'm a nurse, but I don't have
any supplies.


00:18:59.905 --> 00:19:01.372
I'll see what I can do.


00:19:01.707 --> 00:19:05.910
What about you? You are T.I.M
aren't you?


00:19:05.912 --> 00:19:08.479
I am a Transhuman Interactive Machine.


00:19:08.481 --> 00:19:13.251
But my friends call me Tim. I'd be happy 
to assist you in anyway I can.


00:19:13.253 --> 00:19:14.819
Make me a banana split.


00:19:14.821 --> 00:19:17.155
I regret I don't have the
necessary ingredients.


00:19:17.157 --> 00:19:19.023
Yeah, then what good are you?


00:19:19.025 --> 00:19:21.526
Where are we? And how can we
both be on the same planet.


00:19:21.528 --> 00:19:24.128
Hannah, each Ark went to it's
own destination.


00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:26.731
I'm very sorry that I can't
answer your question.


00:19:26.733 --> 00:19:31.235
Whatever caused the ship to crash happened 
before I was scheduled to awaken.


00:19:31.237 --> 00:19:35.439
However, once I was functional I
began recording all ship's telemetry.


00:19:35.441 --> 00:19:42.747
Really? Just before the crash I saw something, 
triangular. It looked like a space ship.


00:19:42.749 --> 00:19:46.918
Yes. I believe I can provide
range and bearing to that target.


00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.687
But exactly what it is, I'm
afraid I can't say.


00:19:49.988 --> 00:19:54.125
Then we have a plan. That ship
could be our ticket home.


00:19:54.127 --> 00:19:57.094
We left earth for a reason. The aliens were
exterminating us!


00:19:57.096 --> 00:19:58.763
<i>What do you think these
aliens are doing?</i>


00:19:58.765 --> 00:20:01.732
We'll find that ship and get
back to earth.


00:20:02.868 --> 00:20:05.703
We've got to get away from here
as far away as possible.


00:20:06.872 --> 00:20:07.805
Right?


00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:09.173
Yeah.


00:20:09.175 --> 00:20:10.508
Yeah.


00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:12.376
Yeah, well you're the one with the gun.


00:20:14.646 --> 00:20:16.781
So how long were you prisoners?


00:20:16.783 --> 00:20:19.984
More like Lab rats. But about 2 years.


00:20:19.986 --> 00:20:21.352
That's not possible.


00:20:21.354 --> 00:20:24.255
I saw the newton leave on TV a month ago.


00:20:24.257 --> 00:20:27.658
I lost counted of the days around 490.


00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:32.129
I was sick for a while. And that
was a while ago.


00:20:32.131 --> 00:20:33.531
All relative.


00:20:33.533 --> 00:20:35.266
How long does a concussion last?


00:20:35.268 --> 00:20:38.236
I believe Captain Crowe
may be less impaired
than he seems.


00:20:38.238 --> 00:20:41.372
He may be trying to convey that 
the elapsed time disparity is due


00:20:41.374 --> 00:20:45.076
to the effects of Einstein's
theory of special relativity.


00:20:45.078 --> 00:20:46.777
I always hated physics.


00:20:46.779 --> 00:20:51.515
Sargent, let's scout at 6. make
sure we are not growing a tail.


00:20:58.991 --> 00:21:01.659
So you're fine flying back to
earth just to get killed?


00:21:01.661 --> 00:21:04.895
I didn't say that. Did I?


00:21:04.897 --> 00:21:08.366
If there is a ship. there's gonna be 
a place on this planet where


00:21:08.368 --> 00:21:10.368
there are no chameleon things are.


00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.769
Like an island or something.


00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:16.340
Yeah. But what if we can't
change their mind?


00:21:16.342 --> 00:21:19.043
Then it's a good thing I'm a pilot.


00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:17.702
Perimeter.


00:22:37.724 --> 00:22:39.590
What the hell was that?


00:22:39.592 --> 00:22:41.158
Let's go find out.


00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:43.427
Sargent! With me.


00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:46.597
Are you ok?


00:22:51.937 --> 00:22:53.804
Stay in a circle.


00:22:59.244 --> 00:23:01.045
Fan out.


00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.434
Where she go?


00:23:40.819 --> 00:23:43.554
It's ok. It's alright. We won't
hurt you.


00:23:44.456 --> 00:23:46.824
It's ok. It's ok.


00:23:49.094 --> 00:23:51.328
She looks almost human. How is
that possible?


00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:54.298
We don't know much about them.
And the cages, they use to
huddle together


00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:58.402
when they weren't being used
for slave labor, or for experiments.


00:23:58.404 --> 00:24:02.173
But I've never seen one like her before.


00:24:30.602 --> 00:24:31.936
It's alright.


00:24:56.761 --> 00:24:59.897
Tastes... like... crap.


00:25:03.168 --> 00:25:04.535
Frank.


00:25:04.537 --> 00:25:06.570
I'm Lea.


00:25:10.976 --> 00:25:12.209
You're ok.


00:25:15.547 --> 00:25:17.114
Where'd they go?


00:25:19.017 --> 00:25:19.984
Where did they go?


00:25:25.156 --> 00:25:26.257
What the hell is that?


00:25:26.259 --> 00:25:27.458
Her name is Lea.


00:25:27.659 --> 00:25:29.159
How do you know her name?


00:25:29.961 --> 00:25:32.763
I... said it... to him.


00:25:34.165 --> 00:25:38.435
The humanoids in the zoo never
spoke. How do you know English?


00:25:38.437 --> 00:25:39.904
I learned... from you.


00:25:39.906 --> 00:25:41.739
From him?


00:25:41.741 --> 00:25:47.645
From all of you. From jungle... I listen you 
in damn cages. You talk a lot.


00:25:47.647 --> 00:25:49.146
She was spying on you.


00:25:49.148 --> 00:25:50.614
We never saw her.


00:25:50.616 --> 00:25:54.952
Can't imagine why. Best damn
camouflage I've ever saw.


00:25:54.954 --> 00:25:57.054
Except for the Chameleons.


00:25:59.991 --> 00:26:02.660
Yeah. We'd better get going.


00:26:02.662 --> 00:26:04.461
No wait where's Honda?


00:26:04.729 --> 00:26:06.297
Not a trace.


00:26:06.932 --> 00:26:10.067
The Captain needs rest. And food.


00:26:10.569 --> 00:26:12.169
Alright, who's got food.


00:26:14.773 --> 00:26:16.106
This is it.


00:26:16.108 --> 00:26:18.976
Food. Food everywhere. I show you.


00:26:20.679 --> 00:26:24.615
Alright. Dug in. We'll get food. 
Give that to Captain Crowe.


00:26:24.617 --> 00:26:26.050
Why you gonna give that to him?


00:26:26.052 --> 00:26:27.585
You're just going to trust her?


00:26:27.587 --> 00:26:29.386
What choice do I have?


00:26:29.388 --> 00:26:30.955
Watch at 6.


00:26:30.957 --> 00:26:35.125
Plus your gun's outta amo. Why
should we follow you?


00:26:37.495 --> 00:26:40.230
Lieutenant Baum's training as
a military officer would have


00:26:40.232 --> 00:26:42.232
included advanced survival tactics.


00:26:42.234 --> 00:26:46.804
As long as Captain Crowe incapacitated, 
he is the logical leader.


00:26:46.806 --> 00:26:49.640
Where is my banana split already?


00:27:03.188 --> 00:27:04.021
Here.


00:27:06.491 --> 00:27:08.125
Good to eat. Sweet.


00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:16.266
No!


00:27:18.003 --> 00:27:21.238
Capelblom. One eat of
those kill a Kormoryx.


00:27:21.439 --> 00:27:22.573
Kormoryx?


00:27:22.575 --> 00:27:24.708
Very big. Very... bad?


00:27:25.043 --> 00:27:26.043
Got it.


00:27:28.380 --> 00:27:29.980
You always fed yourself?


00:27:31.549 --> 00:27:32.783
Always.


00:27:33.018 --> 00:27:35.119
Even when you were little?


00:27:58.543 --> 00:28:00.110
Food.


00:28:13.058 --> 00:28:14.992
-Whoa.Whoa. Whoa!
-Hey!


00:28:21.399 --> 00:28:24.902
If you ever lay a hand on any member of this group
again I'll kick your ass.


00:28:28.873 --> 00:28:30.741
Unless she beats me to it.


00:28:31.776 --> 00:28:33.444
She put the fire out.


00:28:33.446 --> 00:28:36.547
So she saved your ass again. The
fire would have given us away.


00:28:36.549 --> 00:28:40.250
Well I am sorry I don't have your training 
but we can't eat it raw.


00:28:40.252 --> 00:28:42.252
What the hell is this anyway?


00:28:43.955 --> 00:28:46.790
Don't worry. It will taste just
like chicken.


00:28:48.893 --> 00:28:51.095
Hope this spaceship has an oven.


00:28:58.236 --> 00:29:00.137
So what can you tell Chameleons?


00:29:00.139 --> 00:29:02.740
<i>It's not like I've been able to
run tests on them .</i>


00:29:02.742 --> 00:29:06.977
They have technology. Better than ours. 
But they only seem to use it when they have to.


00:29:06.979 --> 00:29:13.684
They keep the humanoids they catch as slaves, 
but they didn't seem to know what to make of us.


00:29:13.686 --> 00:29:17.354
What did they do to you?


00:29:17.356 --> 00:29:20.257
Well, they seem to want to know
if we could inter- -EH!


00:29:21.860 --> 00:29:23.660
Cassie.


00:29:23.662 --> 00:29:25.829
Sorry.


00:29:27.732 --> 00:29:29.333
We're going to get wet.


00:29:29.734 --> 00:29:33.003
I'd be happy to assist in
constructing a rain shelter,


00:29:33.005 --> 00:29:35.806
however I don't believe that was thunder.


00:29:35.808 --> 00:29:38.041
Everybody under cover. Now!


00:29:38.576 --> 00:29:39.409
Come on.


00:29:39.411 --> 00:29:40.944
Oh god.


00:29:48.587 --> 00:29:50.354
No. No.


00:29:50.356 --> 00:29:52.790
Jason!


00:29:56.828 --> 00:29:58.629
What the hell just happen?


00:29:58.631 --> 00:30:02.533
This soil appears rich in
decomposing biological matter.


00:30:02.535 --> 00:30:07.137
It's possible the bombs ignited the methane. 
Higher ground will be safer.


00:30:07.139 --> 00:30:08.672
Still looking like paradise to you?!


00:30:08.674 --> 00:30:10.974
This place ain't perfect but
it's got good air.


00:30:10.976 --> 00:30:14.978
Even better then earth. Food. Water. 
Even the right type of gravity.


00:30:14.980 --> 00:30:17.014
You're forgetting about the Chameleons.


00:30:17.016 --> 00:30:18.682
Tim, which way to the ship?!


00:30:18.684 --> 00:30:22.052
The structure is approximately
ten miles in that direction.


00:30:22.054 --> 00:30:23.954
Let's get off this planet.


00:30:23.956 --> 00:30:26.023
Don't ever try to stop me from
doing something again.


00:30:26.025 --> 00:30:29.960
Lieutenant, as a military officer 
I recognize that you tolerate a higher


00:30:29.962 --> 00:30:34.531
level of risk than the others,
but I cannot allow you, or any human,


00:30:34.533 --> 00:30:40.204
to sacrifice themselves for a
lost cause. Jason was already dead.


00:30:51.817 --> 00:30:55.953
♪ It's a long way to Tipperary.
It's a long way-♪


00:30:55.955 --> 00:30:57.888
Captain.


00:30:57.890 --> 00:31:00.090
Sorry.


00:31:01.192 --> 00:31:02.793
How are you doing?


00:31:03.194 --> 00:31:05.195
How am I doing? Better.


00:31:05.597 --> 00:31:09.366
Thanks for uh- keeping the group moving.


00:31:09.368 --> 00:31:11.134
It's my job but I-


00:31:11.136 --> 00:31:14.738
I had a concussion once... They
asked me my name. I said "Wednesday".


00:31:14.740 --> 00:31:16.506
To bad it was Saturday.


00:31:18.210 --> 00:31:20.410
I wonder what day it is here.


00:31:20.412 --> 00:31:22.312
and what time?


00:31:22.314 --> 00:31:25.115
Well the sun is going down. We
just don't know how long the


00:31:25.117 --> 00:31:27.351
days are. Or the nights.


00:31:28.019 --> 00:31:29.353
Yeah.


00:31:30.889 --> 00:31:34.958
Sergeant, Improvised Weaponry 101.


00:31:34.960 --> 00:31:36.660
Yes sir.


00:31:41.399 --> 00:31:43.500
Do you have any idea where we are?


00:31:43.502 --> 00:31:48.705
Our target was Barnard's Star 4.
But that shouldn't have these rings.


00:31:48.707 --> 00:31:51.541
Something went wrong.


00:31:51.543 --> 00:31:55.512
We were supposed to go to Alpha
Centauri. Three suns there.


00:31:56.681 --> 00:31:59.016
I didn't have time to check the star charts.
Once we came out of


00:31:59.018 --> 00:32:00.984
Cryo we were hitting the atmosphere.


00:32:01.419 --> 00:32:06.757
Frank, Alpha Centauri is the
nearest star system to Earth.


00:32:06.759 --> 00:32:12.129
So wherever we are, we're further 
away then that.


00:32:12.530 --> 00:32:13.664
So-


00:32:13.666 --> 00:32:17.367
So we're talking 40 years. Maybe more.


00:32:19.237 --> 00:32:22.673
Earth is still there. You just find it.


00:32:24.208 --> 00:32:27.344
If it was a ship, yeah I'll find it.


00:32:37.789 --> 00:32:40.023
Your camouflage is incredible.


00:32:40.025 --> 00:32:41.758
"Camouflage"?


00:32:41.760 --> 00:32:42.993
Your um-


00:32:43.361 --> 00:32:45.128
I wish I could disappear like that.


00:32:45.463 --> 00:32:47.597
You want... be like me?


00:32:49.801 --> 00:32:53.670
What What is "get the hell off
this planet"?


00:32:53.672 --> 00:33:00.077
My world was under attack. They bombed us 
from orbit. That we didn't even see it coming.


00:33:01.379 --> 00:33:06.283
Hhmm, your world. Where do you
come from?


00:33:06.285 --> 00:33:11.855
Earth. Far Far Away. Out there.


00:33:12.190 --> 00:33:14.424
Like tell children. Stories.


00:33:14.426 --> 00:33:20.163
Well that's what we thought until they came 
and try to take our world from us.


00:33:23.034 --> 00:33:25.235
And... go back?


00:33:26.904 --> 00:33:28.472
If we can.


00:33:36.147 --> 00:33:37.814
Well, that could be a problem.


00:33:37.816 --> 00:33:40.617
Our destination lies on the
other side of those mountains.


00:33:40.619 --> 00:33:42.819
How did I know you were going to
say that?


00:33:42.821 --> 00:33:46.790
I don't know. Clairvoyance in humans 
is not a well-understood ability.


00:33:48.159 --> 00:33:51.294
Altus Exodus, Frank? huh?


00:34:16.554 --> 00:34:18.622
the others are never going to
make it up here.


00:34:20.391 --> 00:34:22.225
We've got to find an easier way.


00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:30.767
No one else ever do this.


00:34:32.603 --> 00:34:34.671
None of your people use camouflage?


00:34:35.506 --> 00:34:38.175
Not my people. They hide in caves.


00:34:38.876 --> 00:34:42.145
I live in jungle. I hunt,
I kill, I feed. Me alone.


00:34:42.147 --> 00:34:45.282
Ok. What about family?


00:34:45.917 --> 00:34:47.717
No.


00:34:49.821 --> 00:34:51.288
They must be lonely.


00:34:52.156 --> 00:34:53.557
You family?


00:34:53.825 --> 00:34:55.492
On Earth. Maybe.


00:35:04.735 --> 00:35:05.669
You didn't hide.


00:35:05.671 --> 00:35:07.304
No.


00:35:07.306 --> 00:35:10.273
Always something ready to hurt you.


00:35:11.075 --> 00:35:12.409
Remember.


00:35:14.712 --> 00:35:16.113
OK.


00:35:19.250 --> 00:35:20.617
Do you hear that?


00:35:21.552 --> 00:35:22.786
Water.


00:35:40.171 --> 00:35:41.905
Are you sure this water is safe?


00:35:43.541 --> 00:35:45.742
Most of the water on Earth is polluted.


00:35:46.577 --> 00:35:47.677
Polluted?


00:35:47.979 --> 00:35:49.479
Nevermind.


00:36:06.264 --> 00:36:09.032
Do you have any idea where this
water goes?


00:36:09.034 --> 00:36:11.001
Down to ...


00:36:11.003 --> 00:36:14.271
What the word...


00:36:14.273 --> 00:36:15.839
Big Water.


00:36:18.509 --> 00:36:20.644
You mean like a lake or river?


00:36:22.813 --> 00:36:25.215
I'll be right back.


00:36:41.332 --> 00:36:42.632
Hide!


00:37:02.653 --> 00:37:04.621
You really want to say here?


00:37:05.089 --> 00:37:10.894
If those things catch us ...
Honda told me Hannah wasn't sick.


00:37:10.896 --> 00:37:13.730
They impregnated her and she miscarried.


00:37:13.998 --> 00:37:17.801
Like I said, we need to find a
place away from those things.


00:37:18.236 --> 00:37:23.640
In Earth, 12 billion people.
There were still some unhabited Islands.


00:37:23.642 --> 00:37:25.242
We need to find a place like that.


00:37:25.676 --> 00:37:30.113
But there's only 2 of us. And
you're not really my type.


00:37:30.648 --> 00:37:33.750
So we stay alive. We watch each
other's backs.


00:37:34.518 --> 00:37:36.620
The Captain is the only other pilot.


00:37:37.421 --> 00:37:39.656
If something were to happen to him-


00:37:39.658 --> 00:37:42.092
Yeah. Then they need you.


00:37:42.094 --> 00:37:47.664
We could take charge. Fly some
place safe, and just leave.


00:37:47.666 --> 00:37:51.534
It makes sense. The others will
come around.


00:37:51.536 --> 00:37:56.740
Hhhmm, Yeah. That Victoria is
kinda hot.


00:37:56.742 --> 00:38:00.010
We just need to be ready for
"opportunities".


00:38:00.611 --> 00:38:03.847
What's that sound?


00:38:10.187 --> 00:38:14.357
Lieutenant Baum, there is a
Chameleon Airship approaching.


00:38:14.359 --> 00:38:15.792
Please join us in hiding.


00:38:15.794 --> 00:38:16.960
Yeah I know.


00:38:16.962 --> 00:38:21.464
Look, there's a river that will
take us right where we need to be.


00:38:21.466 --> 00:38:23.233
But we've got to make a run for it.


00:38:23.235 --> 00:38:24.768
But they'll catch us.


00:38:24.770 --> 00:38:26.369
Would you for once just shut up
and listen to him.


00:38:26.371 --> 00:38:29.172
We've got to move now! Come on!


00:38:32.576 --> 00:38:34.110
TIM do you float?


00:38:34.112 --> 00:38:38.048
I'm capable of submerged or
surface operation.


00:38:40.017 --> 00:38:41.551
Ahh!


00:38:43.254 --> 00:38:46.656
Get in the water. Stay Submerged
as long as you can. Come on.


00:38:49.593 --> 00:38:51.094
Let the river take you.


00:39:24.395 --> 00:39:26.129
Lieutenant! Here!


00:39:26.131 --> 00:39:28.465
Everyone out! Come on. Let's go!


00:39:47.485 --> 00:39:49.419
Where's Hannah?


00:39:57.862 --> 00:40:00.530
No! No! No!


00:40:00.532 --> 00:40:04.167
Help! Help! Help!


00:40:08.305 --> 00:40:09.639
Come on Peebs.


00:40:33.697 --> 00:40:38.868
We must go. Kormoryx is near.
I can smell it.


00:40:39.236 --> 00:40:42.672
I would be happy to assist by
digging a grave for Hannah.


00:40:42.674 --> 00:40:45.809
Happy? Heartless Son-of-a-


00:40:45.811 --> 00:40:47.911
That's enough. We don't have
time for this.


00:40:47.913 --> 00:40:50.079
We don't have time. Stop. Stop.


00:40:52.516 --> 00:40:56.686
I must apologize if I have offended. 
I'm only here to assist.


00:40:56.688 --> 00:41:02.525
While my form is designed to put you at ease, 
you're correct. I have no heart.


00:41:02.527 --> 00:41:05.829
That's very touching, but aren't we supposed
to be finding the ship?


00:41:05.831 --> 00:41:07.997
What the hell is a Kormoryx?


00:41:07.999 --> 00:41:10.066
Very big. Very Bad.


00:41:12.636 --> 00:41:14.437
We're going to bury her, aren't we?


00:41:15.039 --> 00:41:16.940
We didn't get to bury the others.


00:41:17.975 --> 00:41:20.009
There's nothing left to bury man.


00:41:21.111 --> 00:41:27.116
You know what? We are going to
save humanity. We gotta stay human.


00:41:27.685 --> 00:41:29.652
So we are going to bury her.


00:41:29.654 --> 00:41:31.120
He's right.


00:41:43.868 --> 00:41:46.636
It's an attack ship. It must
have escaped the invasion.


00:41:46.638 --> 00:41:48.671
Looks like they made a
controlled landing.


00:41:48.673 --> 00:41:50.840
Stop Stop Stop.


00:41:55.813 --> 00:41:56.679
Crap!


00:41:56.681 --> 00:42:01.985
It will eat us. All of us! Skin
too tough for spears.


00:42:01.987 --> 00:42:04.120
We need to get inside that ship.


00:42:04.122 --> 00:42:09.759
Well, it's not gonna eat all of
us, will it?


00:42:11.595 --> 00:42:13.062
Would you be happy to assist us?


00:42:13.064 --> 00:42:17.066
Look, just distract it. Get it
to chase you.


00:42:18.936 --> 00:42:21.504
You're not edible. There's
nothing to be afraid of.


00:42:21.506 --> 00:42:26.910
I'm not programmed for fear. But if 
I'm not edible, how will I lure it away?


00:42:28.847 --> 00:42:30.780
Switch clothes with him.


00:42:37.221 --> 00:42:38.821
Shoo.


00:42:44.795 --> 00:42:47.030
Out! Out! damn dragon!


00:42:55.873 --> 00:42:59.809
Everyone. Those are capelblom,
they're poisonous don't eat them.


00:43:22.766 --> 00:43:24.667
Looks pretty good.


00:43:44.121 --> 00:43:44.754
Huh.


00:43:44.756 --> 00:43:46.122
Is it dead?


00:43:46.124 --> 00:43:49.158
I don't know. Keep your fingers crossed.


00:43:57.935 --> 00:44:00.203
We'll have to check the
power cell connections.


00:44:04.842 --> 00:44:08.811
Here. Pull this up. Right here.
Right here. Pull up.


00:44:13.217 --> 00:44:14.384
There she is.


00:44:17.821 --> 00:44:19.322
It looks ok.


00:44:19.324 --> 00:44:21.557
I didn't expect for everything
to work perfectly.


00:44:21.559 --> 00:44:27.497
But these connections are secure. 
It should power the basic system.


00:44:27.499 --> 00:44:33.002
I checked the weapons locker. It's empty. 
But the emergency kit is intact.


00:44:33.004 --> 00:44:35.038
Like it's never been opened.


00:44:35.406 --> 00:44:38.174
They took the weapons and left
all the survival supplies?


00:44:42.513 --> 00:44:43.713
Impossible.


00:44:43.715 --> 00:44:45.581
What?


00:44:45.583 --> 00:44:48.851
I thought an antimatter power cell 
was good for a thousand years?


00:44:48.853 --> 00:44:51.421
Well that's what they say in the handbook.


00:44:52.557 --> 00:44:55.758
Ahh! Hard as a rock.


00:44:56.360 --> 00:45:00.296
Alright lets check every compartment. 
There's gotta be an answer here.


00:45:05.002 --> 00:45:10.540
That's it. No coffee mugs, no old magazines. 
It's like it's fresh from the factory.


00:45:10.542 --> 00:45:12.075
It doesn't make any sense.


00:45:12.077 --> 00:45:14.277
If it was the power cell, could she fly?


00:45:14.279 --> 00:45:16.746
I can't find anything else wrong.


00:45:16.748 --> 00:45:19.415
But we don't have a power cell. It's time to 
figure out how we're going to live here.


00:45:19.417 --> 00:45:20.783
Look man I'm going home.


00:45:20.785 --> 00:45:22.952
Frank, We can't make antimatter here.


00:45:22.954 --> 00:45:26.456
We don't need to make antimatter. Power cell's 
are designed to withstand anything


00:45:26.458 --> 00:45:28.157
Right? Even a crash.


00:45:28.159 --> 00:45:30.493
Yeah it it were to rupture. It
would be "Boom".


00:45:30.495 --> 00:45:33.996
So the AE didn't blow up. Her
power cell is still intact.


00:45:33.998 --> 00:45:36.365
-You don't know what they're like.


00:45:36.367 --> 00:45:37.767
Why not?


00:45:37.769 --> 00:45:39.702
-We're lost.


00:45:39.704 --> 00:45:42.672
You know I'll follow you
anywhere but that sounds crazy.


00:45:42.674 --> 00:45:44.273
Come on man.


00:45:44.275 --> 00:45:47.343
No, Frank. We've been in flight
for a very long time.


00:45:49.146 --> 00:45:51.748
That thing is back. It's got TIM.


00:45:53.217 --> 00:45:54.283
Dammit!


00:45:56.854 --> 00:46:00.289
Alright dragon. Let's find your weak spot.


00:46:26.450 --> 00:46:27.383
Good Job.


00:46:27.684 --> 00:46:29.552
You risked your life to save me.


00:46:29.554 --> 00:46:31.287
You did the same for us.


00:46:31.289 --> 00:46:34.090
I am programmed to assist and
protect humans.


00:46:34.092 --> 00:46:38.027
You risked your life for me. 
For a machine.


00:46:38.029 --> 00:46:40.396
You're more then a machine.


00:46:46.904 --> 00:46:49.172
You are one crazy, heroic,
son of a bitch.


00:47:09.092 --> 00:47:11.527
What is "Altus Exodus"?


00:47:15.132 --> 00:47:22.471
It's a moronic slogan they made up for 
the evacuation, to make it seem less cowardly.


00:47:22.473 --> 00:47:25.208
It means, "The high noble departure".


00:47:31.949 --> 00:47:36.853
In the unit we use to say "Up,
up, and away".


00:47:39.423 --> 00:47:40.623
You risked your life?


00:47:42.459 --> 00:47:46.963
For a member of my unit ... my family.


00:47:53.770 --> 00:47:55.538
It was the right thing to do.


00:47:56.840 --> 00:47:59.876
If we don't protect each other,
we'll all die alone.


00:48:01.879 --> 00:48:03.512
We are family now?


00:48:07.451 --> 00:48:10.353
Do you have other family? 
In your world?


00:48:13.123 --> 00:48:14.557
A ... mate?


00:48:16.560 --> 00:48:18.427
Umm-


00:48:18.429 --> 00:48:20.129
I have a wife.


00:48:22.032 --> 00:48:25.334
She's gone. She left before the attack.


00:48:29.039 --> 00:48:31.207
But I have a daughter.


00:48:31.775 --> 00:48:33.910
She's 5 now.


00:48:39.149 --> 00:48:40.950
Probably older.


00:48:45.789 --> 00:48:47.423
I have to get back to her.


00:48:49.359 --> 00:48:51.594
I promised her I'd be back.


00:48:58.201 --> 00:49:02.405
If we get the power cell,
will you leave?


00:49:04.908 --> 00:49:06.475
You can come with us.


00:49:10.447 --> 00:49:14.984
But that might not happen because without 
anybody's help we're not going anywhere.


00:49:16.286 --> 00:49:17.987
I got your back Frank.


00:49:20.257 --> 00:49:23.025
Me too. Let's get out of here.


00:49:23.860 --> 00:49:25.594
I'm with you Frank.


00:49:28.065 --> 00:49:29.432
I'm in.


00:49:30.968 --> 00:49:33.502
I would be happy to assist you.


00:49:37.874 --> 00:49:39.608
Family.


00:49:43.680 --> 00:49:44.547
Yeah.


00:49:45.882 --> 00:49:47.083
Yeah.


00:49:59.663 --> 00:50:03.332
-Good Morning Cassie.
-Good Morning. Where is Frank?


00:50:03.334 --> 00:50:06.435
I thought we were all going for
the power cell together.


00:50:06.437 --> 00:50:08.571
Frank and Lea went to get water.


00:50:20.917 --> 00:50:22.318
It's beautiful.


00:50:41.071 --> 00:50:43.005
What are you looking at?


00:50:43.007 --> 00:50:44.407
Beautiful.


00:50:46.777 --> 00:50:48.878
Is this a tattoo?


00:50:48.880 --> 00:50:51.113
Some sort of rite of passage?


00:50:51.581 --> 00:50:53.149
Tattoo?


00:50:55.752 --> 00:50:57.219
What?


00:51:05.962 --> 00:51:07.229
Lea?


00:51:08.665 --> 00:51:09.498
Lea?


00:51:10.734 --> 00:51:12.301
Ahh!


00:52:13.330 --> 00:52:14.830
That looks like everything.


00:52:25.008 --> 00:52:25.841
What?


00:52:30.413 --> 00:52:31.847
You all sure about this?


00:52:31.849 --> 00:52:33.182
Come on Frank.


00:52:33.184 --> 00:52:35.217
It's too dangerous. We're leaving.


00:52:35.219 --> 00:52:39.121
Of course we got to get back to AE. 
Without being caught by chameleons.


00:52:39.123 --> 00:52:40.422
Or something worse.


00:52:40.624 --> 00:52:43.726
Yeah. And getting here almost
killed us.


00:52:43.728 --> 00:52:47.530
We should take the river. It will be 
a lot easier than going through that jungle again.


00:52:47.532 --> 00:52:48.931
And probably a lot safer.


00:52:48.933 --> 00:52:50.733
-Well let's say that we get there.
- Right.


00:52:50.735 --> 00:52:53.068
There aren't enough of us for an assault.


00:52:53.070 --> 00:52:55.104
I had an Idea about that.


00:52:55.605 --> 00:52:57.606
Would your people help us?


00:53:16.793 --> 00:53:17.960
Are you alright?


00:53:21.665 --> 00:53:24.266
I'm glad something good has come
out of all of this.


00:53:24.834 --> 00:53:27.403
I think Frank is a very good man.


00:53:30.073 --> 00:53:31.106
What is it?


00:53:31.608 --> 00:53:35.678
What is ... "Tattoo"?


00:53:35.680 --> 00:53:46.488
♪ It's a long was to Tipperary.
To the sweetest girl I know.♪


00:53:46.490 --> 00:53:58.200
♪ Goodbye Piccadilly. Farewell Leicester Square. 
It's a long long way to Tipperary♪


00:53:58.202 --> 00:54:02.538
♪ My heart is still there.


00:54:04.341 --> 00:54:06.976
What does it mean? Tipperary?


00:54:06.978 --> 00:54:08.444
No idea.


00:54:09.012 --> 00:54:10.412
Are we there yet?


00:54:15.151 --> 00:54:17.653
Did you ever consider that the
filed was being bombed?


00:54:17.655 --> 00:54:23.425
If you'd stayed you would have been blown up. 
So in a way I saved your life.


00:54:24.861 --> 00:54:27.696
The village is far bu there is
and entrance near.


00:54:30.267 --> 00:54:31.700
The not used way.


00:54:32.202 --> 00:54:34.270
Back door?


00:54:34.272 --> 00:54:40.242
Back door. Long walk in dark, Under mountain. 
Chameleons don't go underground.


00:54:40.543 --> 00:54:42.044
So we'll be safe inside.


00:54:42.379 --> 00:54:48.417
Never safe. Never all safe. The
people will not want to help us.


00:54:48.885 --> 00:54:52.354
The chameleons hunt them kill them.


00:54:52.356 --> 00:54:55.858
Maybe if we give the Chameleons a bloody nose 
they will leave your people alone.


00:54:55.860 --> 00:54:57.059
Come on. Let's go.


00:54:57.861 --> 00:54:58.794
Stay close.


00:56:02.492 --> 00:56:03.926
There's something back here.


00:56:05.228 --> 00:56:06.528
Just ignore them.


00:56:21.444 --> 00:56:23.412
The village is in the next
cavern.


00:56:24.581 --> 00:56:25.948
I can't go in.


00:56:27.117 --> 00:56:30.786
You know what, we need you to translate.


00:56:40.397 --> 00:56:41.663
What's wrong?


00:56:43.900 --> 00:56:47.803
This is where I use to hide. 
To listen ...


00:56:50.106 --> 00:56:52.674
Sometimes my mother would leave me food.


